      "message": "CodeDictionary needs a destructor to clean up these Entry objects. Or we could consider having an SkArenaAlloc stored on the CodeDictionary? \n\nI kind of like that, since it will keep most Entries together, and autoclean up, but still lets us have the vector and map store Entry* for the random accesses. It\u0027s too bad we can\u0027t have one of the map or vector store plain Entry to manage lifetime, but they would move the data potentially, and SkTBlockList isn\u0027t set up for the index\u0027ed access we want for the uniqueID lookup.",
